@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] scripts-structural-validation-boundary
ADR, runtime-version and contract checkers MUST exit nonzero for failed checks.
Structural validation MUST NOT be reported as proof of design soundness,
contract compliance, physical execution or production availability.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] scripts-fixture-resource-ownership
Acceptance scripts MUST isolate destructive operations to their explicitly
identified fixture databases, services, guest resources and temporary paths.
They MUST verify fixture ownership before deleting persistent VM or database
state, and MUST preserve failure diagnostics without leaking generated secrets.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] scripts-reproducible-releases
Release packaging MUST use the pinned development runtime and include its Nix
runtime closure. Configuration and credentials MUST remain outside the immutable
release artifact; an artifact build alone MUST NOT claim deployment acceptance.
